\ cv8b-nocase.4 - names without case, for the gene nocase (Iteration 497; results/drafts/nocase-496.md).
\ Loaded after cv8b.4 and kfast's and kinput's overlays; each X8 word gives the kernel's word its body, so every
\ caller gets it. Every lookup copies its key to NAMEBUF (NAME>BUF) and every search compares NAMEBUF with the
\ stored names, so folding NAMEBUF after the copy folds every search; HEADER8 folds the name it stores. Only ASCII
\ a-z are folded: other bytes - UTF-8 names among them - stay as they are. Not with klookup, whose (FIND) copies
\ the key in C.
: FOLD8 ( c-addr u --- )  0 ?DO DUP I + C@ DUP 96 > OVER 123 < AND IF 32 - THEN OVER I + C! LOOP DROP ;
: NAME>BUF8 ( c-addr u --- )
\ kfast's: no padding - cv8b.4's SEARCH-WORDLIST8 compares the count and that many bytes; then folded.
  32 MIN NAMEBUF PLACE NAMEBUF COUNT FOLD8 ;
: HEADER8 ( --- )
  32 WORD DUP COUNT FOLD8 DUP C@ 31 > ABORT" name too long" DUP FIND IF ." Redefining: " HERE COUNT TYPE CR THEN DROP DROP
  HERE COUNT CURRENT @ @ HASH 1+ CELLS CURRENT @ + @ HDR-HEAD !
  HDR-HEAD @ IF HERE 3 + HDR-HEAD @ - LINK-LEN ELSE 1 THEN HDR-LEN !
  HERE DUP HDR-LEN @ + HERE C@ 1+ CMOVE>
  HDR-HEAD @ IF HERE HDR-LEN @ + HDR-HEAD @ - ELSE 0 THEN HDR-LEN @ LINK,
  HERE LAST !
  HERE C@ 1+ ALLOT ;
